#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmplayer; is a simple frontend to <application>MPlayer</application>"
", &phonon; and <application>FFMpeg</application>. You can use it for watching "
"all the movie file formats that <application>MPlayer</application>"
", or &phonon; supports as well as watching from <acronym>DVD</acronym>"
", <acronym>VCD</acronym> or <acronym>TV</acronym> and <acronym>camera<"
"/acronym>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The documentation for &kappname; was not finished when &kde; was installed on "
"this computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you need more help, please check <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org\">"
"The &kde; Website</ulink> for updates, or by submitting your question to <"
"ulink "
"url=\"mailto:kde-user@kde.org\">The &kde; User Mailing list</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Team"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "The user interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The application window is made of so called dockable windows. There is always "
"the central view window. Optional there is the playlist window. And finally "
"there is an info window, that just shows itself when some information is "
"there "
"to been shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The playlist window has as of this writing five categories, current item(s), "
"<guilabel>Optical Disks</guilabel>, <guilabel>Television</guilabel>, <"
"guilabel>"
"Persistent Playlists</guilabel> and <guilabel>Most Recent</guilabel>"
". When clicked on a category's text, it will show the contents below this "
"line. "
"Of course there has to be contents, eg. see <link linkend=\"tvsource\"><"
"acronym>"
"TV</acronym> settings</link> for adding content for the <guilabel>"
"Television</guilabel> category. The <guilabel>Most Recent</guilabel> "
"category will fill itself when playing locale media files or network &URL;. "
"This category can hold 60 items of which the last 50 are under the <guilabel>"
"More ..</guilabel> branch."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent Playlists category"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's possible to store your favorite links in the <guilabel>Bookmark<"
"/guilabel> "
"menu, but those are single items. If you want to create a list of items that "
"play after each other, than you should use the <guilabel>"
"Persistent Playlists</guilabel> category."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to add an item in this list is to drag it from <guilabel>"
"Most Recent</guilabel> and drop it on <guilabel>Persistent Playlists<"
"/guilabel>"
". As you will see, when dropped, a pop-up menu appears where you can choose "
"to "
"add to this list or create a new group. Top level items behave like a "
"bookmark "
"item, but items in groups will play the whole group wherein they reside. "
"Items "
"in this category can easily be moved, copied, added to a new group or deleted "
"just by dragging this item to another place in this category. Additionally "
"there are <guimenu>Delete item</guimenu>, <guimenu>Move up</guimenu> "
"and <guimenu>Move down</guimenu> items in the context menu (when clicking "
"with "
"the right mouse button on an item)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course you can add groups to groups to get a deeper hierarchy. When "
"clicked "
"on an item, its group and all its child groups will be copied to the current "
"category and playings starts at the clicked item position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Storage format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The data is stored in "
"<filename>~/.kde/share/apps/kmplayer/playlist.xml</filename>"
", and its format is like this example. See <link linkend=\"XML-editing\">"
"here</link> for manipulating this data directly. <programlisting>\n"
"&lt;playlist&gt;\n"
"    &lt;group title=\"feeds\"&gt;\n"
"        &lt;item url=\"http://www.lugradio.org/episodes.rss\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;item url=\"http://science.nasa.gov/podcast.xml\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;item url=\"http://www.theworld.org/rss/tech.xml\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"    &lt;group title=\"iradio\"&gt;\n"
"        &lt;group title=\"sunny\"&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item mplayeropts=\"-cache 256\" "
"url=\"http://www.swissgroove.ch/listen.m3u\"/&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item "
"url=\"http://www.boombasticradio.com/shoutcast/64.pls\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"        &lt;group title=\"rainy\"&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item "
"url=\"http://www.radioparadise.com/musiclinks/rp_64.m3u\"/&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item url=\"http://www.woxy.com/stream/wma64.asx\"/&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item url=\"http://radionigel.com/winmedia.asx\"/&gt;\n"
"            &lt;item "
"url=\"rtsp://livestreams.omroep.nl/live/vpro/vpro3voor12radioalt.rm\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"&lt;/playlist&gt;\n"
"</programlisting> Also note that for <application>MPlayer</application> "
"custom options can be set using the <computeroutput>mplayeropts<"
"/computeroutput> "
"argument. &kmplayer; searches for this option upwards in the tree, so you can "
"set it for a whole group and override it for a child group or item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Direct &XML; editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current, <guilabel>Television</guilabel> and <guilabel>"
"Persistent Playlists</guilabel> categories can also be manipulated by editing "
"their &XML; storage. Of course one can do that when &kmplayer; is not running "
"and editing the various files in "
"<filename>~/.kde/share/apps/kmplayer/</filename>, but also in the application "
"itself. Simply click on a category label, then choose <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"and next <guimenu>Edit mode</guimenu>. You can also click on a child branch "
"and "
"will then see only the &XML; contents of the branch."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have edited some &XML;, click on the <guilabel>"
"Sync with playlist</guilabel> and either deselect the <guimenu>"
"Edit mode</guimenu> item or click on another catergory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All changes are lost when leaving edit mode or selecting another branch "
"without "
"syncing with playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because of the lazyness of &kmplayer;'s author(s), some features can only be "
"enabled by editing the &XML; ."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Intro/exit animation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Disabling the starting/ending animation can be configured by editing <"
"filename>"
"~/.kde/share/config/kmplayerrc</filename> and modify <programlisting>\n"
"[General Options]\n"
"  No Intro=0\n"
"    </programlisting> the above option to '1'. Just add this option if it's "
"not "
"there yet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's also possible to set an alternative animation. &kmplayer; will look at "
"resp. <filename>~/.kde/share/apps/kmplayer/intro.xml</filename> and <filename>"
"~/.kde/share/apps/kmplayer/exit.xml</filename>. The format has to be a "
"supported &XML; file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The intro animation doesn't have to be a short one, because it will "
"automatically end when another source is opened. Of course for the exit "
"animation this would be a bit annoying, however the user can always end the "
"application twice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A simple example of an intro, showing your favorite photo can be "
"<programlisting>\n"
"&lt;smil&gt;\n"
"  &lt;body&gt;\n"
"    &lt;img dur=\"indefinite\" src=\"file:///home/koos/mum.gif\" "
"fit=\"meet\"/&gt;\n"
"  &lt;/body&gt;\n"
"&lt;/smil&gt;\n"
"    </programlisting> In &kmplayer;'s source package, in the <filename>"
"tests/</filename> are some examples of <acronym>SMIL</acronym> "
"that &kmplayer; supports."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "The backend players"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmplayer; uses external programs to do the actual playing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>MPlayer</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a configuration tab for MPlayer in &kmplayer;'s config dialog. Here "
"you can set MPlayer's path and it cache size for network stream, among other "
"things."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "This player configuration name is <parameter>mplayer</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:212 index.docbook:237 index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Trouble shooting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The best way to debug this backend is to start &kmplayer; from a console "
"application like konsole. Then start a movie with &kmplayer; and see the "
"exact "
"commandline that is used to start mplayer in the console application. Now "
"copy/paste that to another console, remove the '-wid 12344' options, and make "
"it play. Probably it's just choosing the right -ao/-vo params. Also make sure "
"mplayer doesn't start default with a &GUI;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another debugging tool is the 'console' button in &kmplayer;'s toolbar. Here "
"you can see the output from mplayer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Phonon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&phonon; is the &kde; desktop wide multimedia framework and can be configured "
"in &systemsettings;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "This player configuration name is <parameter>phonon</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Basically the same way as trouble shooting <link linkend=\"mplayer-debug\">"
"MPlayer</link>, with the application name of <filename>kphononplayer<"
"/filename>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browser plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is no configuration tab for this player in &kmplayer;'s config dialog. "
"Everything must be configured by manually editing the <filename>"
"~/.kde/share/config/kmplayerrc</filename> like with configuring the <link "
"linkend=\"backend-mimetype\">backend per mimetype</link>"
". This is an example how to let flash be played with the swfdec-mozilla "
"plugin:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[application/x-shockwave-flash]\n"
"player=npp\n"
"plugin=/usr/lib/mozilla/plugins/libswfdecmozilla.so"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can play flash inside &kmplayer;, actually you can even paste the special "
"<parameter>embed</parameter> field for <ulink url=\"http://www.youtube.com\">"
"YouTube</ulink> in the <link linkend=\"XML-editing\">playlist &XML;</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to let &kmplayer; play flash in HTML pages, you should make the "
"&kmplayer; plugin the service provider for the <parameter>"
"application/x-shockwave-flash</parameter> mimetype in &kde;'s <guilabel>"
"File Associations</guilabel> configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As in the above example, this player configuration name is <parameter>"
"npp</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Start &konqueror; or &kmplayer; in a console application and look for errors "
"about loading the browser plugin library. The process started is called "
"<filename>knpplayer</filename>. If that doesn't give any errors, check the "
"backend output capturing inside &kmplayer; (<guimenu>View</guimenu>"
", <guimenuitem>Console</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>Console</guimenuitem> "
"from the popup menu)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Force backend player for a mimetype"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure to always use a given backend for a particular mimetype (if "
"detected of course) can be done by manually editing the <filename>"
"~/.kde/share/config/kmplayerrc</filename>. For example, let phonon play all "
"ogg "
"files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[audio/ogg]\n"
"player=phonon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "The playable sources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmplayer; can play from various sources. These sources are listed in the "
"Source menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>TV</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmplayer; can play from TV cards using <application>MPlayer</application> "
"or <acronym>XVideo</acronym> (using <application>kxvplayer</application>"
"). Before you can watch TV, you have to configure which device to use and the "
"TV channels. You can use the scanner from the configure dialog for this or "
"edit "
"the config file manually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The config file for TV settings is a &XML; file, located <filename>"
"~/.kde/share/apps/kmplayer/tv.xml</filename>. See <link "
"linkend=\"XML-editing\">"
"here</link> for manipulating this data directly. The &XML; format is like "
"this "
"example: <programlisting>\n"
"&lt;tvdevices&gt;\n"
"    &lt;device path=\"/dev/video0\" width=\"320\" height=\"240\" name=\"BT878 "
"video (Hauppauge (bt878))\" audio=\"\"\n"
"              minwidth=\"48\" minheight=\"32\" maxwidth=\"924\" "
"maxheight=\"576\" playback=\"0\" xvport=\"240\"&gt;\n"
"        &lt;input name=\"Television\" id=\"0\" tuner=\"1\" norm=\"PAL\" "
"xvenc=\"0\"&gt;\n"
"            &lt;channel name=\"Ned1\" frequency=\"216\"/&gt;\n"
"            &lt;channel name=\"VCR\" frequency=\"594.90\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;/input&gt;\n"
"        &lt;input name=\"Composite1\" id=\"1\" xvenc=\"7\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;input name=\"S-Video\" id=\"2\" xvenc=\"14\"/&gt;\n"
"        &lt;input name=\"Composite3\" id=\"3\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/device&gt;\n"
"    &lt;device path=\"/dev/video1\" width=\"640\" height=\"480\" "
"name=\"Philips "
"740 webcam\" audio=\"\"\n"
"              minwidth=\"160\" minheight=\"120\" maxwidth=\"640\" "
"maxheight=\"480\" playback=\"1\"&gt;\n"
"        &lt;input name=\"Webcam\" id=\"0\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/device&gt;\n"
"&lt;/tvdevices&gt;\n"
"</programlisting> Note that <quote>input</quote> elements having channels, "
"should have the <quote>tuner</quote> attribute set to <quote>1</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>XVideo</acronym> only uses the <quote>xvport</quote> and <quote>"
"xvenc</quote> attributes and they can only be set by manually editing this "
"file. The values of these two attributes can be retrieved by running <quote>"
"kxvplayer</quote> in a terminal application like <quote>konsole</quote>"
". For every port, <quote>kxvplayer</quote> will output lines like below and "
"the "
"numbers can be set for the attributes mentioned. <programlisting>\n"
"    xvport 240\n"
"    ....\n"
"    encoding: 0 PAL-television\n"
"    encoding: 1 NTSC-television\n"
"    encoding: 2 SECAM-television\n"
"    ....   \n"
"</programlisting> Also width and height attributes are ignored by the <"
"acronym>"
"XVideo</acronym> player. This player gets the sizes from the X server. One of "
"the nice things of <acronym>XVideo</acronym> is that scaling is done in "
"hardware, by the video card, so fullscreen support without CPU usage and "
"without resolution change of your monitor. Also no annoying flicker when "
"another window overlaps this video window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the VDR section for more information about using <acronym>XVideo</acronym>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>VDR</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure your VDR settings in &kmplayer;, see the Configure panel->"
"Source->"
"VDR->XVideo port panel. There should be ports detected, from which you should "
"select one. You have to figure out what encoding you should use (eg. for "
"western europe, that is PAL) and likely the correct one has a name with <"
"quote>"
"dvb</quote> in it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For instance, I have a TV card, a DVB-S card and a webcam plugged into my "
"system. With these, my settings are that there are three Ports. The first one "
"has a long list of NTSC(-JP)/PAL(-M)/SECAM entries all saying something about "
"television/composite/svideo (my TV card). The second one has "
"NTSC-dvb/PAL-dvb/SECAM-dvb (my DVB-S card). And finally the third has only "
"ntsc/pal (probably my webcam). I should therefore configure (just select it) "
"the second port and second entry (PAL-dvb)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because VDR support from &kmplayer; can only use <acronym>XVideo</acronym>"
", of course <acronym>XVideo</acronym> should work (and I believe for video "
"devices, this way of viewing only works on linux). Also this only works on "
"your "
"first display (:0.0). So make sure <quote>videoforlinux</quote> "
"extension works with the X server. For the XFree86 server, therefore in its "
"configuration (<filename>/etc/X11/XF86Config</filename>) it should have"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Section \"Module\" \n"
"     .... \n"
"     Load    \"v4l\" \n"
"EndSection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, when ever you update your video driver, you have to "
"reconfigure "
"this setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commandline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Internally for the sources, &kmplayer; uses distinct names. At the time of "
"this "
"writing these are \"dvdnavsource\", \"dvdsource\", \"exitsource\", "
"\"introsource\", \"pipesource\", \"tvscanner\", \"tvsource\", \"urlsource\", "
"\"vcdsource\" and \"vdrsource\". When activated, they mostly starts playing "
"the "
"list of playable items."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can activate a particular source with a <filename>kmplayer://</filename> "
"type <acronym>URL</acronym>. Just set the host part as the source name and "
"optional path part as extra arguments, so for a channel for the \"vdrsource\" "
"this could look like <filename>kmplayer://vdrsource/22 MTV 2</filename>"
". Eg. this script starts &kmplayer; using \"dvdnavsource\" and using &DBus; "
"to "
"play fullscreen. <programlisting>\n"
"/bin/bash\n"
"kmplayer kmplayer://dvdnavsource/ &amp;\n"
"PID=$!\n"
"sleep 2\n"
"qdbus org.kde.kmplayer-$PID /kmplayer/MainWindow_1 showFullScreen\n"
"    </programlisting> For some sources this will not do much because they are "
"not meant to be for normal playing. For \"pipesource\" this is disabled "
"because "
"that would be a bad security hole of course."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions, Answers, and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any hints to make my CDROM less noisy when playing from it (not VCD://)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sure, try <command>hdparm -E 8 /dev/cdrom</command> as root after mounting "
